  <data name="SatsInfo.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Understanding Satoshis (Sats) and Bitcoin</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SatsInfo.Body1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bitcoin is a decentralized digital currency, where each unit is divisible into smaller fractions called Satoshis, or 'Sats.' A single Satoshi, named after Bitcoin's enigmatic creator, Satoshi Nakamoto, is the smallest unit of Bitcoin, equating to 0.00000001 BTC. This makes 100 million Satoshis equal to one Bitcoin.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SatsInfo.Body2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>By breaking Bitcoin into these tiny units, users can make microtransactions and participate in Bitcoin’s economy with even the smallest amounts of value.</value>
  </data>
